Subject: select-v2: the selected option shows its check mark

What: the option's check svg carries `ui-select-v2-option-check`, and a selected
option draws it at full opacity and scale.
Why: select-v2 renders its options as menu-v2 items, and menu-v2.css starts every
indicator svg transparent, scaled to 0.25 and blurred, revealing it only under
`[data-checked]`. Kobalte's select marks a chosen option `[data-selected]`, never
`[data-checked]`, so the chosen option's check never appeared. Keyed by class,
not by the bare svg.

diff --git a/src/v2/components/select-v2.css b/src/v2/components/select-v2.css
index 3c88d0d759..9fc3445547 100644
--- a/src/v2/components/select-v2.css
+++ b/src/v2/components/select-v2.css
@@ -288,3 +288,9 @@
 .ui-select-v2-option:not([data-selected]) .ui-select-v2-option-indicator {
   visibility: hidden;
 }
+
+.ui-select-v2-option[data-selected] .ui-select-v2-option-check {
+  opacity: 1;
+  scale: 1;
+  filter: none;
+}
